Ambassador Jeffrey Bartos
U.S. Representative for U.N. Management and Reform
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Madam President. And thank you to ASG Khiari and Director Connell for your briefings.
The United States is deeply concerned by the recent attacks in Kramatorsk and Pryluky.
Colleagues, as President Trump has strongly condemned the unnecessary loss of life in this war, and he has been clear that the killing must stop.
Kyiv and Moscow should make the responsible choice and immediately return to the negotiating table, not extend this carnage and its impacts well beyond the front lines.
We also call for all parties to take immediate steps to strengthen protection of humanitarian workers. Recent attacks affecting medical facilities, humanitarian evacuations, logistics, and aid workers are unacceptable. We recognize the humanitarians who put themselves in harm’s way to try to help civilians in need and demand their protection.
The conflict will not end through military victory for either side, but only through negotiations.
The United States will continue to work towards a swift and durable end to the war through our support for ceasefire and negotiated settlement.
The sooner Ukraine and Russia can reach agreement, the fewer people will die on both sides.
Around the world, this conflict is depriving people of life-saving grain and other food.
We will play whatever constructive role we can, including our continued mediation of trilateral talks, to bring an end to this senseless war. We expect the same of Ukraine and Russia.
